Z||000000||SLYGUY||10-05-2001||04:24 PM||||Hey there...<P>I replaced the EGR and just replaced the O2 sensor. I always disconnect the battery for a minute or two to reset the computer and I am still running rich and coating the rear with soot.<P>Does this have to do with the fact that I have yet to change the plugs, distributor cap and rotor? I'd also like to replace the fuel filter and run a couple of bottles of fuel injector cleaner through. What else can I do?<P>Will the plug change and cap/rotor help eliminate this embarassment?<P>As usual, your help is greatly appreciated.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-05-2001||05:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Hey there...<P>I replaced the EGR and just replaced the O2 sensor. I always disconnect the battery for a minute or two to reset the computer and I am still running rich and coating the rear with soot.<P>Does this have to do with the fact that I have yet to change the plugs, distributor cap and rotor? I'd also like to replace the fuel filter and run a couple of bottles of fuel injector cleaner through. What else can I do?<P>Will the plug change and cap/rotor help eliminate this embarassment?<P>As usual, your help is greatly appreciated.<P>Sly<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Sly!<BR>A general tune up may help, but it sounds more like time to replace injector(s)?<BR>How does the car drive?<BR>Six or four?<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||10-05-2001||07:33 PM||||My car did that! it was do do do..leaky injectors man! it sucked..but the car ran bad to not the same power..etc..bad gas millage.<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||03:22 AM||||Well...<P>I was thinking that the car had a fuel system adjustment problem, and it does, but I think the problem may lie a little deeper.<P>On the way to work a couple of days ago, the oil pressure guage was dancing a little bit, and if you took a corner hard the needle would dive into the red and the light would flash till you straightened out. When I got home, it took TWO quarts to register on the dipstick. I just changed the oil and filter two months ago and have drive twenty-five hundred miles since. <P>The car is burning oil I think. This would explain why it smokes momentarily on startup (more if it doesn't catch right away) and if you start it after it has ran, then sat for 20 mins.<P>Running the STP fuel injector cleaner through, changing the fuel filter, plugs, cap and rotor will help it run better but not cure the oil comsuming problem. <P>What a bummer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||03:24 AM||||FieroWrecker...<P>It's the 2.8<BR>102K miles<BR>5spd<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||03:26 AM||||I still have an occasional lope in the idle. Sometimes great, sometimes not. I'm fairly sure this will be remedied with the tuneup since I've changed sensors.<BR>Engine runs strong. Doesn't smoke except occasional startup like I've mentioned.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||03:50 AM||||I know what I'm gonna do.<P>I'm just gonna do the complete tuneup, and pay to have the valve guides/seals replaced.<P>This sucks!<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||10-06-2001||07:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>I know what I'm gonna do.<P>I'm just gonna do the complete tuneup, and pay to have the valve guides/seals replaced.<P>This sucks!<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Check your area, there may be a shop that does heads and will trade heads with you for $100 per head...<BR>Then you will have reconditioned heads and a strong running car...<BR>But after all that, six stock injectors may be the answer to the rich running...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||SKIDMARK||10-06-2001||11:24 AM||||I hate to be a doomsayer but if your going through that much oil, you must have more than bad valve seals. Sounds to me like maybe a little blow-by. Oil burning will cause a greasy soot to form on the back of your nice white car (voice of experience). Have someone follow you and check for blueish smoke and burning oil smell from your exhaust. Also check your compression. A new PCV might help things a little but in the long run, it may be time to rebuild. Or maybe get that 3.4 you've been dreaming about.||||reg||1
Z||000009||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||09:00 PM||||I pulled a plug and took it down to Autozone. Bought the Bosch Super plugs, distributor cap and rotor. Under $20!<P>The plugs on the far side weren't as hard to replace as I thought. A swivel ratchet helps a lot here. Plugs looked like hell! Nothing obvious, just looked burnt and old. Guy at Autozone said that the plugs I pulled out were not the right depth (4 banger plugs).<P>The cap and rotor were in extremely poor condition. Suprised it ran at all. <P>With new plugs, cap and rotor the motor isn't spitting little clumps of fuel at idle like before and is purring like a kitten. I think the soot problem is solved, but not the valve stem seals.<P>I have a noisy throwout bearing, so when I have the clutch and that bearing replaced soon, and they have the engine out I'm gonna have the valves, seals, and head gasket replaced. Will have very little to worry about after that.<P>Thanks for the help!!<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000010||SLYGUY||10-06-2001||09:05 PM||||I meant that the plugs WERE the right depth. If they weren't they would of made swiss cheese of the pistons. The plugs I removed were burnt because they were the wrong temperature.<P>With the most recent tuneup it is running like new. Smooth and strong.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rick 88||10-07-2001||12:24 AM||||Sly,<P>Have you checked the inside of your exhaust tips to see if the are excessively wet? 102k does not seem like enough miles to be worn like that. Have you changed your PCV valve?<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||5
Z||000012||SLYGUY||10-07-2001||12:29 AM||||Yes, I have checked the inside of my exhaust tips. Besides the being dusted with black dust, they appear okay. NO moisture. <P>Damn, the PCV is the ONLY sensor that I haven't replaced. I pulled it out of the knuckle on the valve cover and it looked awfully fresh. New in fact. I thought that was good at the time, but hey, can the tube be blocked further up? <BR>Would that cause you to consume/burn oil.<P>You are right about the motor. At 102K the motor is running extremely well. I changed the plugs, cap and rotor and you'd swear you were in someone elses car. It feels like I gained 15 horses or something. <BR>Idles so well you could set a watch to it. No smoke when you rap the throttle to 5K repeatedly. Won't stumble under any circumstances.<BR>PCV huh?<BR>Give me more info!<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
